#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:1
msgid ""
"Decide how pyvista-wasm executes PyVista filters on top of the vtk-wasm "
"pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:3
msgid "Status: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:4
msgid "Date: 2026-02-14"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:5
msgid "Decision-makers: tkoyama010"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:7
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:9
msgid ""
"PyVista's filter API (`clip`, `decimate`, `smooth`, `contour`, ...) is a "
"thin Python wrapper over VTK's pipeline: each filter is a `vtkAlgorithm` "
"whose output ports feed the renderer. pyvista-wasm drives the same VTK "
"code compiled to WebAssembly (VTK.wasm), where "
"`VTK::CommonExecutionModel` — the module defining algorithms, ports, and "
"the pipeline — is available with serialization coverage ([vtk-wasm "
"roadmap](https://kitware.github.io/vtk-wasm/roadmap/)). However, the "
"pyvista-wasm renderer bridge (`ts/renderer.ts`) builds scenes as a flat "
"list of actors with a `source` per actor, and some algorithm classes are "
"not registered with the VTK.wasm `vtkDeserializer` in the rendering-mode "
"binary — `vtkShrinkPolyData` is a known example, worked around with a "
"hand-written JavaScript implementation. Issue "
"[#778](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/778) asks how "
"pyvista-wasm should execute PyVista filters on top of the available "
"`VTK::CommonExecutionModel` classes. Which execution strategy should "
"pyvista-wasm adopt?"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:11
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:13
msgid ""
"**PyVista parity**: filter methods should behave like their PyVista "
"counterparts without Python-side reimplementation drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:14
msgid ""
"**Upstream availability varies**: some `vtkAlgorithm` classes are not "
"deserializable in the current VTK.wasm binary, so a strategy that "
"requires every filter to be a wasm pipeline object fails for those "
"filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:15
msgid ""
"**Renderer simplicity**: the bridge must stay auditable; a scene format "
"that grows an unbounded set of bespoke cases is a maintenance liability."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:16
msgid ""
"**Testability**: the strategy must be verifiable in pytest (mock "
"renderer) and Playwright (browser) without flaky visual assertions."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:18
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:20
msgid ""
"**Option A: Prefer wasm pipeline objects, fall back to documented manual "
"implementations (hybrid)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:21
msgid ""
"**Option B: Always serialize real `vtkAlgorithm` chains and require "
"upstream to register every filter**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:22
msgid ""
"**Option C: Reimplement all filters in pure Python/NumPy and never use "
"the wasm pipeline**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:24
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:26
msgid ""
"Chosen option: **Option A — hybrid, prefer the wasm pipeline, fall back "
"to manual implementations**."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:28
msgid ""
"When a filter class is registered with the VTK.wasm deserializer, "
"pyvista-wasm serializes it as a `source` filter chain in the scene data "
"and lets VTK.wasm execute it (this is how `clip`, `tube`, and `contour` "
"work today)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:29
msgid ""
"When a filter class is unavailable upstream, pyvista-wasm implements it "
"manually in the renderer bridge (as `shrink` already does), and the "
"filter's docstring documents the manual implementation so the workaround "
"can be removed when upstream registers the class."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:30
msgid ""
"Each new filter lands one at a time with a mock-renderer test asserting "
"the serialized scene data and, where practical, a Playwright browser "
"test."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:32
msgid ""
"This keeps PyVista parity for the most filters at the lowest maintenance "
"cost, degrades gracefully where the wasm binary is incomplete, and gives "
"every filter a documented upgrade path to a real pipeline object."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:34
msgid "Positive consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:36
msgid ""
"Filters ship incrementally without blocking on upstream VTK.wasm "
"registrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:37
msgid ""
"The scene format stays flat and auditable; no bespoke pipeline graph "
"format is introduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:38
msgid ""
"Missing upstream deserializer registrations are easy to inventory (search"
" for the documented manual implementations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:40
msgid "Negative consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:42
msgid ""
"Manual fallbacks can drift from VTK semantics until upstream classes "
"become available; each carries a documented ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:43
msgid "Two execution paths mean two test surfaces per filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:45
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0015-decide-how-pyvista-wasm-executes-pyvista-filters-on-top-of-the-vtk-wasm-pipeline.md:47
msgid ""
"The strategy is already validated by the shipped filters: `clip`, `tube`,"
" and `contour` exercise the wasm pipeline path, and `shrink` exercises "
"the manual fallback path. Both paths are covered by `tests/test_mesh.py`."
msgstr ""

